"533",""
"534","Qays ibn Talq narrated from his father Talq ibn Ali, who said: ""We went out as a delegation of six to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), five from Banu Hanifah and one man from Banu Dab'ah ibn Rabi'ah, until we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). We pledged allegiance to him and prayed with him, and we informed him that we had a church in our land, and we asked him for some of his leftover ablution water. He called for water, performed ablution from it and rinsed his mouth, then poured it for us into a water skin. Then he said: 'Go with this water, and when you arrive at your land, break down your church, sprinkle its place with this water, and make its place a mosque.' We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, the land is far and the water will dry up.' He said: 'Add water to it, for it will only increase it in goodness.' So we went out and disputed over carrying the water skin — which of us would carry it? The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) made it a rotation among us, for each man among us a day and a night. So we went out with it until we arrived at our land, and we did what he commanded us. The monk of that day was a man from Tayy. We called the adhan for prayer, and the monk said: 'A call of truth,' then he fled and we never saw him again."""
