"572",""
"573","ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah narrated from his father, from his grandfather Qatādah ibn al-Nuʿmān, who said: ""It was a night of intense darkness and rain. I said to myself: 'Would that I took advantage of this night to attend the ʿIshāʾ prayer with the Prophet ﷺ!' So I did. When the Prophet ﷺ finished the prayer and turned to leave, he noticed me while he was walking with a dried palm-stalk (ʿurjūn) in his hand. He said: 'What brings you here at this hour, O Qatādah?' I replied: 'I took advantage of attending the prayer with you, O Messenger of Allah.' He gave me the palm-stalk and said: 'Indeed, Satan has stayed behind in your home. Go with this palm-stalk, hold onto it until you reach your house, then take it from behind the house and strike with it.' I left the mosque, and the palm-stalk lit up like a candle, giving light by which I walked. I came to my family and found them asleep. I looked into the corner and found a hedgehog there. I kept striking it with the palm-stalk until it went out."""
"574","On the authority of Sālim, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: I was a young, unmarried man during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so I used to sleep in the mosque. Whoever among us saw a dream would relate it to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). So I said: ""O Allah, if there is any good for me with You, then show me a dream that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) will interpret for me."" I fell asleep and saw two angels come to me; they took me along. Another angel met them and said: ""Do not be afraid."" Then they took me to the Fire, and behold, it was folded up like the folding of a well, and there were people in it whom I recognized some of them. Then they took me to the right side. When morning came, I mentioned that to Ḥafṣa. Ḥafṣa claimed that she related it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he said: ""ʿAbdullāh is a righteous man; if only he would pray more at night."" He said: So ʿAbdullāh used to pray more at night."
"575","On the authority of Salim, from Ibn Umar, who said: I was a young, unmarried man during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), so I would stay overnight in the mosque. Whoever among us saw a dream would narrate it to the Prophet (peace be upon him). I said: ""O Allah, if there is any good for me with You, then show me a dream that the Prophet (peace be upon him) may interpret for me."" So I slept and saw two angels coming to me; they took me away. Another angel met them and said: ""Have no fear."" Then they took me to the Fire. Behold, it was folded up like the folding of a well, and therein were people whom I recognized some of. Then they took me to the right side. When morning came, I mentioned that to Hafsa. Hafsa reported that she had narrated it to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), and he said: ""Abdullah is a righteous man, would that he prayed more at night."" He (the narrator) said: So Abdullah used to pray more at night."
"576",""
"577","Abu Hurairah reported: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Prayer has a beginning and an end. The beginning of the time for the Zuhr prayer is when the sun passes its zenith, and its end is when the time for the Asr prayer enters. The beginning of the time for the Asr prayer is when its time enters, and its end is when the sun turns yellow. The beginning of the time for the Maghrib prayer is when the sun sets, and its end is when the twilight disappears. The beginning of the time for the Isha prayer is when the twilight disappears, and its end is when half the night has passed. The beginning of the time for the Fajr prayer is when dawn breaks, and its end is when the sun rises."""
