"699","Al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh narrated from his father, who said: I asked Aisha about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family), how he used to pray. She said: He would pray Al-Hajir (the midday prayer), then pray two rak'ahs after it, then pray Al-Asr, then pray two rak'ahs after it. I said: But Umar used to strike people for them and forbid them? She said: Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to pray them himself, and he knew that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) used to pray them. But your people, the people of Yemen, are a people of Tugam (ignorant/foolish); they would pray Zuhr, then pray what is between Zuhr and Asr, then pray Asr, then pray what is between Asr and Maghrib. So Umar struck them, and he did well."
