"723","Abu Qatadah narrated: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) on a journey. He said: ""If you do not reach water tomorrow, you will suffer thirst."" So the swift ones among the people hurried off seeking water, but I stayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). The Prophet's mount leaned to one side, and the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) dozed off. I propped him up, and he straightened. Then he leaned again, and I propped him up, and he straightened. Then he leaned until he almost fell off his mount, so I propped him up, and he woke up. He said: ""Who is the man?"" I said: ""Abu Qatadah."" He said: ""Since when have you been traveling?"" I said: ""Since last night."" He said: ""May Allah protect you as you protected His Messenger."" Then he said: ""Shall we camp?"" So he leaned toward a tree and dismounted. He said: ""Look, do you see anyone?"" I said: ""This is a rider, these are two riders,"" until they reached seven. We said: ""Guard our prayer for"
"724","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) while he was praying at the end of the night. So I prayed behind him. He took me by the hand, pulled me, and made me stand beside him. When the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) turned to his prayer, I stepped back. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) prayed, and when he finished, he said to me: ""What is the matter with you?"" (In another narration: ""What is wrong with you?"") ""I place you beside me and you step back?"" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, is it appropriate for anyone to pray beside you while you are the Messenger of Allah whom Allah has given?"" He said: ""So he was pleased with me and supplicated to Allah for me to increase me in knowledge and understanding."" Ahmad added: ""Then I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) sleep until I heard him breathing heavily, then Bilal came to him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! The prayer.' So he stood up and prayed without renewing his ablution."""
"725",""
"726","On the authority of Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""Whoever believes in Allah and His Messenger, establishes the prayer, and fasts Ramadan, it is a right upon Allah to admit him into Paradise, whether he strives in the cause of Allah or sits in the land in which he was born."" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Shall we not give glad tidings to the people?"" He said: ""Indeed in Paradise there are one hundred degrees which Allah has prepared for those who strive in His cause; the distance between each two degrees is like the distance between the heaven and the earth. So when you ask Allah, ask Him for Al-Firdaws, for it is the middle of Paradise and the highest part of Paradise — and I think — above it is the Throne of the Most Merciful, and from it spring forth the rivers of Paradise."""
