"763","Jabir ibn Abdullah reported: While the Prophet ﷺ was delivering the Friday sermon, a caravan arrived in Medina, and the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ rushed toward it until only twelve men remained with him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, if you had continued to leave until not one of you remained, the valley would have flowed with fire for you."" Then this verse was revealed: ""And when they see merchandise or amusement, they disperse toward it and leave you standing"" (Al-Jumu'ah: 11). It is said that among the twelve who remained steadfast with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were Abu Bakr and Umar."
